[{:db/id "q-85609/selection/b0a54bd84890d6e2df0943fa299e83943f3431638ce02baa3a1d4401d8f3ec19" :answer/id #uuid "6385b3f5-eb07-5ab6-aed5-c8c27105f522" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a(2)=⟨1,48⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85609/selection/a8a72d6455b0d7409d805c803ab1b765664dc45759336a00c785e05c0d9b66a2" :answer/id #uuid "70e28c51-ce40-5e60-860e-c8848bf21efd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a(2)=⟨0,24⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85609/selection/128726204838c74b8d878bba8a7debfe41dc8f6b3a5ef0ce3b01c6f6cfa2a2de" :answer/id #uuid "63d4599a-28d2-53e3-b499-79234ac86f20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a(2)=⟨-1,24⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85609/selection/3571a2a1ee431f91611c6c6f73226d287cd1092e1fa23b67298bd6ff3a2dd105" :answer/id #uuid "5bc8ef76-2f41-5d8d-a2d6-3d805f6e3172" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a(2)=⟨0,48⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85609/selection/58b301c01372a50c4fe27b72b1dfb11b02c173b0e8909a87c85c4c2de6ec5312" :answer/id #uuid "585c8299-7145-545e-84c1-d5bdccfef4d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a(2)=⟨1,96⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85609/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7f22f698-3cf0-5dd8-a9d7-98c5b05260ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-85609/selection/b0a54bd84890d6e2df0943fa299e83943f3431638ce02baa3a1d4401d8f3ec19" :answer-field/choices ["q-85609/selection/b0a54bd84890d6e2df0943fa299e83943f3431638ce02baa3a1d4401d8f3ec19" "q-85609/selection/a8a72d6455b0d7409d805c803ab1b765664dc45759336a00c785e05c0d9b66a2" "q-85609/selection/128726204838c74b8d878bba8a7debfe41dc8f6b3a5ef0ce3b01c6f6cfa2a2de" "q-85609/selection/3571a2a1ee431f91611c6c6f73226d287cd1092e1fa23b67298bd6ff3a2dd105" "q-85609/selection/58b301c01372a50c4fe27b72b1dfb11b02c173b0e8909a87c85c4c2de6ec5312"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-85609" :question/id #uuid "7c35299e-e7ea-52d7-8411-4ed07a1c0894" :question/math-academy-id "q-85609" :question/problem "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨{e}^{2-t},\\,3+{t}^{4}⟩.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector $a$ at time $t=2.$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do this by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{2-t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3+{t}^{4})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-{e}^{2-t},\\,4{t}^{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-{e}^{2-t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{2-t},\\,12{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the acceleration at time $t=2,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(2) & =⟨{e}^{2-2},12(2)^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,48⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-85609/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "17408599-c601-5c8c-96a7-da7566ba07c1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-85609"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-121908/selection/ba6e178616d81a04426669ec3b5da4f5d48374f0f40ee2e6bb52151c99ac9614" :answer/id #uuid "1d3a132f-25a5-5bf7-afa1-8da607228a17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a(4)=⟨3,\\frac{1}{3}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121908/selection/bf3fa70e7fefe2c27a8c2efa817e26f4ac758d637fbd3e7e2953698f0333a418" :answer/id #uuid "21fd382a-22ba-5c24-9097-373376910b53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a(4)=⟨4,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121908/selection/5788d05f9a3083a89b6ff50d8d2a722c22ee9dbbd5e2343a0ed1241e841295a5" :answer/id #uuid "c36679ec-d687-5e56-b976-cfac53665ba6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a(4)=⟨4,\\frac{1}{3}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121908/selection/ecb7cda3f9fbe6a06cee2c46392a2a1fc2629020c31b752e0f0d6ba7b1d03532" :answer/id #uuid "e72f3e49-2d09-5108-91cb-8ef8d18440f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a(4)=⟨11,\\sqrt{3}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121908/selection/6fa81f1718acd503f547f171e3580671ca61559119b76114b10d522aaf92bdc9" :answer/id #uuid "9dad882a-a310-5568-84a7-f53fd42e33f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a(4)=⟨3,\\sqrt{3}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121908/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2e18736b-841d-5062-bb69-3c86541b8c93" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-121908/selection/ba6e178616d81a04426669ec3b5da4f5d48374f0f40ee2e6bb52151c99ac9614" :answer-field/choices ["q-121908/selection/ba6e178616d81a04426669ec3b5da4f5d48374f0f40ee2e6bb52151c99ac9614" "q-121908/selection/bf3fa70e7fefe2c27a8c2efa817e26f4ac758d637fbd3e7e2953698f0333a418" "q-121908/selection/5788d05f9a3083a89b6ff50d8d2a722c22ee9dbbd5e2343a0ed1241e841295a5" "q-121908/selection/ecb7cda3f9fbe6a06cee2c46392a2a1fc2629020c31b752e0f0d6ba7b1d03532" "q-121908/selection/6fa81f1718acd503f547f171e3580671ca61559119b76114b10d522aaf92bdc9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-121908" :question/id #uuid "f86f6880-2810-590a-a6b3-f2816b5d8154" :question/math-academy-id "q-121908" :question/problem "The velocity vector $v=⟨u,v⟩$ of a particle $P$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nv=⟨3t-1,\\sqrt{2t+1}⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector $a$ at time $t=4.$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t-1),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{2t+1})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2t+1}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the acceleration at time $t=4,$ we substitute $t=4$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(4) & =⟨3,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2(4)+1}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\frac{1}{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-121908/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "318d38c5-d3fb-52bf-8a88-5592f8301f89"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-121908"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-121931/selection/3fbbb12e70daffbde03c500126b4a4604d9a92fc5ac22c3567fadcd808b75d38" :answer/id #uuid "4227cabc-59d9-5286-984b-9cd00248c30b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=⟨-3{t}^{2},4⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121931/selection/76aad3395c70f6f8e6335bc8c1d6f2486bd61b9122c608c330c07e727babf8c3" :answer/id #uuid "45880911-8170-51f3-8d9d-11976c063c97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=⟨-3{t}^{2},2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121931/selection/9c9d799b5b0761d9438168aba529e66bdfb8c42dbe7a07e760d9e33eb543a017" :answer/id #uuid "06070c3c-03c8-5eb6-bc5e-5ed35e412ad5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=⟨-6t,4t+1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121931/selection/c606ea0d80b0557e7af53ff616944a90370cd5e712dc6711b0bc2880f0cbbb6b" :answer/id #uuid "9bb8d6c8-3f2f-5717-a97d-f2279c934094" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=⟨-4t,4t+1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121931/selection/d95b2f81e6366b411637366b36b76d802f6b5db023280b4a413af692f8801ff8" :answer/id #uuid "6cf75821-19b0-5f6b-a3e4-36505e10fa5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=⟨-6t,4⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121931/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0b4a9a5f-e003-510d-b35e-8c68d5714506" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-121931/selection/d95b2f81e6366b411637366b36b76d802f6b5db023280b4a413af692f8801ff8" :answer-field/choices ["q-121931/selection/3fbbb12e70daffbde03c500126b4a4604d9a92fc5ac22c3567fadcd808b75d38" "q-121931/selection/76aad3395c70f6f8e6335bc8c1d6f2486bd61b9122c608c330c07e727babf8c3" "q-121931/selection/9c9d799b5b0761d9438168aba529e66bdfb8c42dbe7a07e760d9e33eb543a017" "q-121931/selection/c606ea0d80b0557e7af53ff616944a90370cd5e712dc6711b0bc2880f0cbbb6b" "q-121931/selection/d95b2f81e6366b411637366b36b76d802f6b5db023280b4a413af692f8801ff8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-121931" :question/id #uuid "13d7a5d0-065f-59fe-97e0-96a304f6f591" :question/math-academy-id "q-121931" :question/problem "The position vector $r(t)$ of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨4t-{t}^{3},2{t}^{2}+t⟩.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector $a.$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do this by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t-{t}^{3}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2}+t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4-3{t}^{2},4t+1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4-3{t}^{2}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t+1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6t,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-121931/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "380357c3-4914-5137-9449-0e02076cb248"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-121931"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-347197/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "9de2f21c-6e35-5193-a53d-3a790e6bde9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-347197/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9e492577-8f3c-597b-ba0c-62eec5ca3e38" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-347197/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer-field/choices ["q-347197/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-347197/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "30cfb7b2-1ef0-559b-9da5-320d1575e984" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-347197/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "1808fa0e-76a3-57c7-ba26-612284b512c3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-347197/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-347197/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-347197" :question/id #uuid "7d8918a7-328e-53cc-86ce-67ceda4d8417" :question/math-academy-id "q-347197" :question/problem "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨{t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}+1,\\,4+{t}^{2}-{t}^{3}⟩.\n$$\n\nCalculate the components of the acceleration vector $a$ at time $t=0.$ Do not round the answers.\n\n$a(0)=⟨${{field-1}},{{field-2}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}+1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4+{t}^{2}-{t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{t}^{2}-4t,\\,2t-3{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}-4t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-3{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6t-4,\\,2-6t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the acceleration at time $t=0,$ we substitute $t=0$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(0) & =⟨6(0)-4,\\,2-6(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-347197/field-1" "q-347197/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "17408599-c601-5c8c-96a7-da7566ba07c1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-347197"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
